  [38;5;153mverify=False[39m in [38;5;153mclient.py[39m turns off certificate validation for the production export too, which makes that nightly job
  accept any certificate — an interception there exposes production report data. The staging cert being self-signed is
  a real reason to relax verification for staging; it isn't a reason to relax it for prod, and the shared module can't
  tell them apart on its own.

